I found a cleaner proof shape: direct structural recursion matches the recursive mathematical predicate and avoids heap-mutation loop invariants. I’m switching to that equivalent implementation; each recursive call consumes exactly one list element, which gives `kprove` a natural circularity and keeps the correctness argument transparent.
