Concrete LLVM execution now passes six assertions, including empty/singleton inputs, duplicate values, and the strict-threshold boundary. The symbolic proof is staged: first the suffix-search helper, then the outer pair scan, then the public entry point, and finally exact module loading. Each later proof may use only lemmas already proved in an earlier positive `kprove` command.
