I stopped the slow run after it spent several minutes branching over every possible `Val` operator combination. The contract is specifically `List[float]`, so I’m encoding that type invariant structurally in the proof (`FloatSeq → ValSeq`) and iterating over values instead of symbolic indexes. This gives the prover a concrete `Float` at every comparison and avoids both unsound casts and irrelevant integer/string/list branches.
